two","html_url":"https://github.com/taketwo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-20T15:45:18Z","updated_at":"2016-09-20T15:46:37Z","body":"Unfortunately, this is still not fixed in master. Here is a simple way to reproduce. In the root of \"glm\" repository paste the following into a \"test.cu\" file:\n\n``` cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include \"glm/gtx/io.hpp\"\n\nint main(int argc, const char** argv)\n{\n  glm::vec3 v;\n  std::cout << v;\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nThen compile: `nvcc -c test.cu`. You should get tons of warnings of two types:\n- `a __host__ function redeclared with __host__ __device__, hence treated as a __host__ __device__ function`\n- `calling a __host__ function from a __host__ __device__ function is not allowed`\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/248342252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"taketwo","id":1241736,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDE3MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1241736?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo","html_url":"https://github.com/taketwo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taketwo/followers","follo